Save the visible helper/main as main.go and the test below as main_test.go in a module. Run go test -count=1 to avoid using a cached test result. The if initializer got := Twice(3) binds got for the condition and body of that if. The comparison asks whether Twice(3) actually returns six; the successful main print alone is not the test.
```go
package main
import "testing"
func TestTwice(t *testing.T) {
 if got := Twice(3); got != 6 { t.Fatalf("got %d, want 6", got) }
}
```
